---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import GroupedBarChart from '../components/GroupedBarChart.astro';
---
<BaseLayout title="Data & Results — VIOT Research" page="data" description="Erosion campaign, EBS lifetime analysis, and Fowler-Nordheim breakdown risk.">
  <div class="container">
    <section class="hero">
      <p class="hero-eyebrow">Results</p>
      <h1>Data &amp; Findings</h1>
      <p class="hero-sub">Primary erosion campaign, electron-backstreaming lifetime analysis, and Fowler–Nordheim breakdown risk assessment. All 36 runs fully reproducible from <code>VIOT3/campaign_results.json</code>.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <div class="section-inner">
        <div class="section-label-col">
          <h2 class="label">Erosion Campaign</h2>
          <p style="font-size:0.8rem;color:var(--muted);font-family:var(--font-mono);line-height:1.5;margin-top:1rem;">36 runs<br>3 materials<br>4 throttles<br>3 seeds<br>N=1e5<br>DX=10 µm<br>5,000 steps</p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <p class="label">Comparative erosion — atoms sputtered per run</p>
          <div class="table-wrap" data-gsap="table">
            <table>
              <thead>
                <tr>
                  <th>Throttle</th>
                  <th>I_b (A)</th>
                  <th>Mo (atoms)</th>
                  <th>GNP (atoms)</th>
                  <th>Graphene (atoms)</th>
                  <th>GNP LEF</th>
                  <th>Graphene LEF</th>
                </tr>
              </thead>
              <tbody>
                <tr>
                  <td>TH0</td><td>0.51</td><td>6.827e10</td><td>1.740e10</td><td>1.841e11</td>
                  <td class="td-navy">3.92×</td><td class="td-bad">0.37×</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                  <td>TH5</td><td>0.84</td><td>1.124e12</td><td>2.657e11</td><td>1.988e12</td>
                  <td class="td-navy">4.23×</td><td class="td-bad">0.57×</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                  <td>TH10</td><td>1.10</td><td>4.435e12</td><td>1.579e12</td><td>6.293e12</td>
                  <td class="td-navy">2.81×</td><td class="td-bad">0.70×</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                  <td>TH15</td><td>1.76</td><td>3.730e13</td><td>2.679e13</td><td>4.404e13</td>
                  <td class="td-navy">1.39×</td><td class="td-bad">0.85×</td>
                </tr>
              </tbody>
            </table>
          </div>
          <p style="font-size:0.8rem;color:var(--muted);font-family:var(--font-mono);margin-top:0.75rem;">GNP LEF = Mo erosion / GNP erosion. Values &gt;1 mean GNP reduces erosion. Values &lt;1 for Graphene mean graphene <em>worsens</em> erosion. CV &lt; 0.57% across all 12 cases.</p>
          <GroupedBarChart
            caption="Lifetime-extension factor vs. throttle — GNP reduces erosion, graphene worsens it"
            categories={["TH0", "TH5", "TH10", "TH15"]}
            series={[
              { name: "GNP LEF", colorClass: "s1", values: [3.92, 4.23, 2.81, 1.39] },
              { name: "Graphene LEF", colorClass: "s2", values: [0.37, 0.57, 0.70, 0.85] },
            ]}
            unit="×"
          />
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section>
      <div class="section-inner">
        <div class="section-label-col">
          <h2 class="label">EBS Lifetime</h2>
          <p style="font-size:0.8rem;color:var(--muted);font-family:var(--font-mono);line-height:1.5;margin-top:1rem;">10 seeds<br>N=2e5<br>TH10<br>NX=117<br>Barrier depth<br>1091.15 V</p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <p class="label">Electron-backstreaming lifetime factor (LEF_EBS)</p>
          <div class="table-wrap" data-gsap="table">
            <table>
              <thead>
                <tr>
                  <th>Coating</th>
                  <th>φ_m (V)</th>
                  <th>dφ_m/dr (V/m)</th>
                  <th>dr/dt (m/s)</th>
                  <th>dφ_m/dt (V/s)</th>
                  <th>LEF_EBS</th>
                </tr>
              </thead>
              <tbody>
                <tr>
                  <td>Mo (baseline)</td><td>8.95</td><td>7.367e5</td><td>4.309e-8</td><td>3.148e-2</td>
                  <td>1.0×</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                  <td>GNP</td><td>8.95</td><td>7.367e5</td><td>3.270e-9</td><td>2.389e-3</td>
                  <td class="td-navy">13.18×</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                  <td>Graphene</td><td>8.85</td><td>7.367e5</td><td>6.382e-8</td><td>4.702e-2</td>
                  <td class="td-bad">0.669×</td>
                </tr>
              </tbody>
            </table>
          </div>
          <p style="font-size:0.8rem;color:var(--muted);font-family:var(--font-mono);margin-top:0.75rem;">Internal cross-check: dφ_m/dr = 736,719.386 V/m identical to machine precision across all three coatings — validates that LEF_EBS differences come purely from erosion rates. 95% CI widths: ~0.5% of mean.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section>
      <div class="section-inner">
        <div class="section-label-col">
          <h2 class="label">Breakdown Risk</h2>
          <p style="font-size:0.8rem;color:var(--muted);font-family:var(--font-mono);line-height:1.5;margin-top:1rem;">Fowler–Nordheim<br>Weibull model<br>NSTAR nominal<br>≈1.9 MV/m</p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <p class="label">Fowler–Nordheim vacuum breakdown — Weibull parameters</p>
          <div class="table-wrap" data-gsap="table">
            <table>
              <thead>
                <tr>
                  <th>Material</th>
                  <th>φ (eV)</th>
                  <th>Weibull λ</th>
                  <th>Weibull k</th>
                  <th>Onset (P&gt;1e-4)</th>
                  <th>P_BD @ 15 MV/m</th>
                </tr>
              </thead>
              <tbody>
                <tr>
                  <td>Mo</td><td>4.6</td><td>100</td><td>2.0</td>
                  <td>7.27 MV/m</td><td>0.15</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                  <td>Graphene</td><td>4.5</td><td>150</td><td>1.8</td>
                  <td class="td-accent">4.01 MV/m</td><td class="td-accent">0.44</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                  <td>GNP</td><td>4.5</td><td>200</td><td>1.5</td>
                  <td class="td-bad">2.26 MV/m</td><td class="td-bad">0.58</td>
                </tr>
              </tbody>
            </table>
          </div>
          <p style="font-size:0.8rem;color:var(--muted);font-family:var(--font-mono);margin-top:0.75rem;">NSTAR nominal inter-grid field ≈ 1.9 MV/m. Rim field enhancement β ~2–10 for machined edges, ~70 for sharp nanostructures — can push local field into the 2.3–7.3 MV/m divergence band.</p>
          <GroupedBarChart
            caption="Vacuum-breakdown onset field by material — lower is riskier"
            categories={["Mo", "Graphene", "GNP"]}
            series={[
              { name: "Onset field", colorClass: "s1", values: [7.27, 4.01, 2.26] },
            ]}
            unit=" MV/m"
          />
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section>
      <div class="callout">
        <p class="accent-label">Summary</p>
        <h2>GNP wins on erosion. GNP is risky on breakdown.</h2>
        <p>GNP reduces erosion 1.39–4.23× and extends EBS-limited life up to 13.18×. Its edge-rich morphology drops breakdown onset from 7.3 to 2.3 MV/m — partially negating the benefit. Graphene is actively harmful at all throttles: it adds an erosion channel and shortens EBS life to 0.669×.</p>
      </div>
    </section>
  </div>

</BaseLayout>
